s","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"04bb6da97f8d89362a258142a7b3a7afb2fd783888d6cb78a15d83c0c2ebc3a7"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:G6","usage":{"input_tokens":105753,"output_tokens":2816,"requests":7}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"6b9128b19498b1a0030702daeaab4d515014de95bc7a6187ccef8465557d61fe"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T3","usage":{"input_tokens":12836,"output_tokens":872,"requests":2}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"c029b52c907fb7f1adc66c7a296790dd179b8ff92e4416b7b75c7bc04d682e81"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T1","usage":{"input_tokens":67949,"output_tokens":1903,"requests":4}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"1baeb205fc04995b090abfd753f8595a77a546aca9a258b9e9c4b19408dfb32a"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:project.symbol-reference-completeness","usage":{"input_tokens":6943,"output_tokens":597,"requests":1}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"b1fabcef40ab21ea8a9c9b45a47b78e6f921bed8f5f499e89c38d7c4fa16d86c"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T8","usage":{"input_tokens":25890,"output_tokens":1391,"requests":2}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"89cd43f19272bb395b1a5feb6dda52937e8460240afe0439409db2d10a029b86"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T5c","usage":{"input_tokens":34357,"output_tokens":1841,"requests":3}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"28c21be04700232e28dfbe7b1e987d3bae726b24fd2dacf6126cc0a5d9c5d7b1"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T10","usage":{"input_tokens":78031,"output_tokens":2725,"requests":5}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Record the concrete prevention/detection mechanism for AC7 (e.g., a CI gate that blocks apply from non-main refs, or a drift-alert that fires on unlanded-state divergence) with a change id / config location, matching the evidence rigor of AC5/AC6.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2","F1","E1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC7: 'The root cause is addressed, not just the instance: applying to production from an unlanded branch is what created a state/HCL divergence... Record how that is prevented or detected.'","AC7 checkbox is [x] but no attestation/mechanism is recorded inline, unlike AC5's 'landed as 1b3bf5ffd1f' and AC6's 'Dispatched run 35580537296'."],"finding":"AC7 is marked [x] but records no actual prevention/detection mechanism; unlike AC5 (which cites change id 1b3bf5ffd1f) and AC4/AC6, AC7 states only the requirement ('Record how that is prevented or detected') with no recorded content, so the root-cause remedy is unspecified.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3c5752bdd870a983","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria / AC7","norm_id":"n2fb889efa8960a7f","priority":0.75,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer cannot confirm the divergence class is prevented; a future out-of-band apply from an unlanded branch could recreate the same silent state/HCL drift."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Record, in the plan under AC7, the concrete mechanism that prevents or detects a production apply from an unlanded branch (e.g. apply gated to landed `main` only, or a scheduled state-vs-`main` reconciliation check), rather than only asserting the root cause is addressed.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC7: 'The root cause is addressed, not just the instance: applying to production from an unlanded branch is what created a state/HCL divergence that took days to surface. Record how that is prevented or detected.' — marked [x] but no mechanism is stated in the plan body.","T9 concurrency/ownership: 'Update concurrency / ownership is clear' — the divergence arose because state was mutated (apply) from a source (unlanded branch) with no ownership discipline tying apply to landed main."],"finding":"AC7 requires recording HOW applying-from-an-unlanded-branch is prevented or detected in future, but the plan text never states the actual prevention/detection mechanism even though the AC is marked complete. The root failure is a shared-state ownership/atomicity gap: production apply was allowed to write Terraform state from HCL that had not landed on main, creating a state/HCL divergence with no owner and no detection until the drift lane surfaced it days later. Without recording the concrete guard (e.g. applies gated to only run against landed main, or a state-vs-main reconciliation check), the same divergence can recur silently.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7da6d715d887880d","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC7","norm_id":"n3237d604851e8fc2","priority":0.75,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State the guard explicitly: e.g. 'terraform apply in CI runs only on merged main; a scheduled drift job (this lane) now alerts on any non-empty plan, so a state/HCL divergence is detected within one schedule tick.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Under AC7, name the concrete guard that prevents/detects production applies from unlanded branches (e.g., the scripts/terraform_prod.py origin/main currency check, or a CI gate on the drift lane) and cite where it lives, so the root-cause-addressed claim is verifiable.","cohort":["T10"],"criteria":["T10"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.275,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC7 text: 'The root cause is addressed, not just the instance ... Record how that is prevented or detected.' — the mechanism itself is not stated.","A repo wrapper scripts/terraform_prod.py enforces _ensure_current(repo, remote='origin', branch='main', fetch=True) before writing a saved prod plan (tests/unit/test_terraform_prod_wrapper.py lines 35-37), which would be a fitting mechanism to cite — but the plan does not reference it.","T10(c) idempotency & drift: out-of-band manual changes (CLI apply from an unlanded branch) are exactly the drift-inducing action this AC must show is prevented/detected."],"finding":"AC7 is marked satisfied but the plan text never states the concrete prevention/detection mechanism for 'applying to production from an unlanded branch'; it only restates the requirement ('Record how that is prevented or detected'). Without naming the guard, the root-cause claim is unverifiable and the drift class is not demonstrably closed.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa203a3a2b28d6c40","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — AC7","norm_id":"n3c49d210da70a8fd","priority":0.625,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer signing off cannot confirm the state/HCL divergence class is actually prevented, only that the current instance was reconciled — the same failure could recur.","A future engineer applies from another unlanded branch and reproduces the identical drift because no gate was recorded."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Amend AC7 to state the mechanism explicitly, e.g. 'Prevented by scripts/terraform_prod.py, which refuses to produce a prod plan/apply unless the working tree is current with origin/main (_ensure_current, remote=origin, branch=main); covered by tests/unit/test_terraform_prod_wrapper.py.' Add whether it is enforced in CI or only advisory.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Broaden AC2's currency detection to also catch non-'$' representations (e.g. add alternation for 'USD', 'dollars', and '$ ' with whitespace) before asserting the check returns nothing.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.5375,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC2: \"Checked: `git log origin/main -p <files> | grep -nE '\\$[0-9]'` returns nothing.\"","Publication constraint: 'monetary figures do not go into committed guidance or history' — broader than the '$NNN' shape."],"finding":"AC2's proving command `grep -nE '\\$[0-9]'` only detects currency written with a leading '$' immediately followed by a digit; it would miss amounts expressed as 'USD 500', '500 dollars', or '$ 500' (with a space), yet the publication constraint targets any 'literal currency amount'.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff3857ebe05d024ac","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria / AC2","norm_id":"n7b200171547340b9","priority":0.4125,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A currency amount rewritten as 'USD 500' in a commit message or README survives the AC2 check and lands in public history."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Use `grep -nEi '\\$[[:space:]]*[0-9]|[0-9][[:space:]]*(usd|dollars?)|usd[[:space:]]*[0-9]'` as the AC2 anchor.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["2 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","AC item 'AC1 The spend-cap HCL is present on `main`, landed through Gerrit per `CONTRIBUT' cites operational evidence (merge_gate) that lives outside the codebase; tag it [non-codebase] — prefix the checkbox text with [non-codebase] so the completion verifier accepts a recorded attestation instead of failing to find code proof.","AC item 'AC3 The landed HCL matches the live resources, so `terraform plan` proposes zero' cites operational evidence (iac) that lives outside the codebase; tag it [non-codebase] — prefix the checkbox text with [non-codebase] so the completion verifier accepts a recorded attestation instead of failing to find code proof.","AC item 'AC7 The root cause is addressed, not just the instance: applying to production f' cites operational evidence (prod) that lives outside the codebase; tag it [non-codebase] — prefix the checkbox text with [non-codebase] so the completion verifier accepts a recorded attestation instead of failing to find code proof."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"f0119583e455dde5","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["a57e512a3c04e80e",4962],"description_boxes":["7b70d3ab4c764154",7],"file_impact":["d3140811aa2f973e",12],"ticket_id":["7f4205d83e0f211f",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":288292,"cache_write_tokens":166189,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; the fast claim check is a local HMAC verify)","det_ms":5227.8,"input_tokens":478851,"llm_calls":30,"llm_ms":214387.0,"output_tokens":22536,"precheck":{"cited_anchor_warning":false},"total_ms":233760.7,"verify_requests":11},"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","priority_floor":0.8,"provider_provenance":{"candidates":["bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6"],"capabilities":{"native_structured_output":true,"prompt_cache_style":"bedrock","supports_temperature":true,"supports_thinking":true,"web_access":"off"},"endpoint_host":null,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","provider":"bedrock","ran_model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","region":"us-east-1","region_source":"repo-c